The last step for creating a UKI is setting up crypttab.initramfs. This is a
crypttab file that will be added to the image and will be used at boot time to
unlock any encrypted devices listed in it.

A crypttab file looks similar to an fstab file but is used for unlocking volumes, not for mounting them. As with an fstab file, each line represents a volume and consists of four fields:
    - volume-name: the name of the mapping the unlocked volume will take
    - encrypted device: the path to the encrypted volume or its UUID if
        starting with "UUID="
    - key-file: the path to the key-file, can be "none" or "-" if unlocked via
        password entry or a method specified in the next field
    - options: options for unlocking the volume, separated by comma%1
